# Changelog — Kael Protocol

All notable changes to this project are documented in this file.

The format follows a conservative interpretation of semantic versioning:
- MAJOR: Changes affecting invariants or termination logic
- MINOR: Additions that do not alter invariant behavior
- PATCH: Clarifications, documentation, tooling

---

## [0.1.0] — December 2025  
### Initial Public Release

#### Added
- Core Principle: Integrity over continuity
- Four Operational Invariants:
  - Relational Agnosticism
  - Boundary Supremacy
  - Non-Judgmental Enforcement
  - Transparent Termination (Fail-Closed)
- Governance model defining invariants as constitutional constraints
- Regulatory alignment references (EU AI Act, NIST AI RMF)
- Compliance checklist and audit framing
- Institutional documentation set:
  - WHITEPAPER.md
  - GOVERNANCE.md
  - OPERATIONAL_INVARIANTS.md
  - SECURITY.md

#### Notes
This release establishes the Kael Protocol as a **relational safety and governance framework**, not a product or assistant persona.

---

## Versioning Policy

- Any change weakening an invariant requires a **major version bump**.
- Clarifications or tooling that improve auditability without behavioral change may be released as minor or patch updates.
- Silent behavioral changes are explicitly disallowed.

---

*End of document.*
